id.instance: String (TS "c<n>")
num.game: i32
num.cursor: u32
map.ordered: IndexMap
bag.data: IndexMap<String, serde_json::Value>
error.style: Result<_, EngineError> with TS's message; panic only on invariants (refusal-string checks such as why_cannot_activate_ability are Result<(), EngineError>)
null.optional: Option + skip_serializing_if
null.nullable: Option, serialised null
case.json: camelCase via serde rename_all
case.rust: snake_case
state.mut: &mut GameState writes, &GameState reads, &mut EngineSink for TS sink mutators
rng.source: Rng::new(&state.seed, state.rng_cursor) and write the cursor back (the tests' own sinkFor does not write it back, as TS's did not)
hook.style: Arc<dyn Fn(&mut EffectContext) -> Vec<Effect> + Send + Sync> via hook(); triggers via TriggerDef::new; no fn pointers, no Box
registry.style: OnceLock set once by register_all; fused scripts built on lookup from state; tests use the testkit's thread-local register_scripts over registered_scripts().clone()
async.style: tokio in crates/server only; none in pure crates
log.style: tracing JSON to stdout, server only
test.scenario: jackioh_cards::register_all() then testkit::scenario(json!); card refs are &str (catalog id, index, name or instance id)
test.live_objects: owned CardInstance copies; re-read with s.card(&id), write with find_instance_mut
test.state_mut: Scenario::state_mut(&mut self) -> &mut GameState for TS's writes through s.state
test.expect_style: expect_* take &self
test.literals: setups, play options, effect args and fixture CardDefs as json!/json_as of TS's literals
